(7194821, 1106945, 129147, '<td valign="top">I don''t think that the clouds have a great impact on this scene as the foreground greens are terrific and seem to take center stage for me. I enjoy the shot, 7.</td>', 'I don''t think that the clouds have a great impact on this scene as the foreground greens are terrific and seem to take center stage for me. I enjoy the shot, 7.', '2014-03-27 15:50:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(7194849, 1106613, 98339, '<td valign="top">What I see first is all the noise/grain in your picture.  To me it seems that it is more noise vs grain.  A noise reduction filter would go a long way.<br/> <br/>Not sure what time of the day this was taken but I don''t think at night/evening as the headlights are not on, on the vehicles.  Obviously this was taken through the windshield and there are small water dots/flairs near the sun (but not "spots").<br/> <br/>The tilt of the horizon bothers me...I like to see level pictures (unless it''s a tilt challenge...duh).  And just sometimes a tilted picture works but not here.<br/> <br/>Overall the picture seems to be very underexposed (dark) and quite a bit of detail is lost in that darkness.  But your caption of the clouds definitely meets the challenge.<br/> <br/>I think that this is a redeemable image and has potential.  But you need to watch some of the tutorials that I suggested to get your "ahhh haaaaa" moment.<br/> <br/>I hope that helps.</td>', 'What I see first is all the noise/grain in your picture.  To me it seems that it is more noise vs grain.  A noise reduction filter would go a long way. Not sure what time of the day this was taken but I don''t think at night/evening as the headlights are not on, on the vehicles.  Obviously this was taken through the windshield and there are small water dots/flairs near the sun (but not "spots"). The tilt of the horizon bothers me...I like to see level pictures (unless it''s a tilt challenge...duh).  And just sometimes a tilted picture works but not here. Overall the picture seems to be very underexposed (dark) and quite a bit of detail is lost in that darkness.  But your caption of the clouds definitely meets the challenge. I think that this is a redeemable image and has potential.  But you need to watch some of the tutorials that I suggested to get your "ahhh haaaaa" moment. I hope that helps.', '2014-03-27 17:56:32.000000', NULL, 1),
